  "title": "CJP Alleges Delay in Release of Leaders, Four Sureties Rejected",
  "summary": "The Congress for the Progressive Movement (CJP) alleges that leaders Saurav Das and Ashutosh Ranka were held in judicial custody for five days after their entry into Jantar Mantar, a protest site, despite the designation of the location as a protest site. A legal action is being taken against those responsible for their detention.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "CJP has accused the authorities of deliberately delaying the release of Saurav Das and Ashutosh Ranka for five days due to their involvement in a protest at Jantar Mantar in Delhi.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The four sureties involved in their custody were rejected from further legal custody.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The CJP is seeking legal action against those responsible for their detention in a broader context of political tensions and judicial delays.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
